WEBVTT

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.510
<b>Looking for lost cat.</b>

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.520
Ta-dah!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.080
A cat?

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.480
Yeah.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.260
I thought I could at least help other people a bit with my magic,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.410
so I had Misa-san construct a cat-searching Code for me.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.580
There!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.520
Huh?

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.310
Nothing's happening.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.390
I would think a Code that Misa-san made would have some effect.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.000
Why a wash basin?

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.400
I imagine you changed it into that yourself.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.910
I didn't!

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:16.030
The Code did it on its own.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.270
Let me try.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.090
If it's just executing a magical Code on a computer,

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.180
I should be able to do it, as well.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.980
I'm just pressing a button.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.290
Y-Yeah.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:27.780
There.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.410
See?

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.910
You're right...

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.720
I believe that it's definitely this one.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.160
Yeah.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.390
All I have to do is turn off the power.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.490
Let's go see its owner.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.340
Y-Yeah.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.880
If you have a computer that can execute magic,

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.270
then anyone can use Modern-Day Magic.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.750
Misa-san is the one who wrote the Code.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.090
Kaho-chan was the one who ran it.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.470
In the end, I did nothing...

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.340
I wonder what I need to do to get better at magic...

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.970
I know!

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.080
An item?

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.480
Yeah!

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.470
I want to hurry and improve, to be like Misa-san and Yumiko-chan.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.520
So I was thinking I need an item

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.620
like Misa-san's amulet or Yumiko-chan's staff.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.610
I see. And what were you thinking of specifically?

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.700
Huh?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.600
Did you decide what item you were going to get?

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.040
I haven't yet...

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.220
I thought about a lot of different ones, though.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.130
In that case, why don't we look for one after school?

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.170
Are you sure? Thanks, Kaho-chan!

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.900
I wonder what item I should get...

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.670
Kaho-chan, what do you think?

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.940
How about the Magma Staff or the Fairy Flute?

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:41.980
Huh?

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.420
If you don't understand, that's fine.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.180
Ah, it's you two.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.440
Oh, Yumiko-chan.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.410
I was about to go to Misa-san's house.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.820
Sorry, we're going shopping today,

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.800
so we won't be heading to her place.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.000
Th-There's not really any reason to apologize...

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.950
Where are you going shopping?

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.140
We haven't decided yet.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.990
Yeah, what should I do...

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.380
How about Shibuya?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.720
There's something I want to get.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.000
If you're heading to Shibuya, I'll go with you!

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:36.160
Th-There are a lot of people... A lot... A lot...

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.460
Morishita, are you all right in this crowd of people?

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:43.520
Yeah, I'm going to find an item.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.780
I have to do my best.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.250
Let's go.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.770
Oh, wait!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.010
It smells like roses!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.550
Wow, they're that much...

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.660
That'll be five hand creams.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.040
She has a lot of money!

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.830
There are lots of them.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.090
This might be good.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.440
Wow.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.800
What should I do? What should I do?

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.980
This is cute!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.140
I wonder if it would look good.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.310
I think you should try it on.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.450
Kaho-chan, could you take a look?

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.330
Sure.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.370
It's too big...

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.620
What do you think?

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.560
I guess God isn't fair.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.770
Look at this!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.510
I decided on him.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:26.640
It's Mr. Turtle!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.370
I don't think you should call him "Mr. Turtle."

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.650
Decided on?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.440
What do you mean?

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:37.820
I thought I'd make him my magical item.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:39.260
Magical item?

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.300
She was searching for an item like you two have,

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.780
something like your staff and Misa-san's amulet.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.310
I want to get better at magic so I can be like you two,

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.510
so I got this turtle and-

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.020
I don't approve!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:04.210
Do you think Misa and I are good at magic because we use tools?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:05.830
You're completely mistaken

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:09.080
if you think just anyone can be good at magic simply by having tools.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.750
U-Um... I...

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.990
I've misjudged you.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.680
There we go.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.030
It's done.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.860
You should be able to use some Codes now.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.950
Thank you.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:45.490
Well, Yumiko's just like that.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.560
She'll be harsh at times.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.420
Don't worry about it too much.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:51.840
Yeah.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.400
She was right, though.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.140
Hm?

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.950
Somewhere in my heart,

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:24.560
I thought I'd be able to improve at magic just by getting an item.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.230
I guess you could expect her to get mad.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.470
It's human to use tools.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.770
Sometimes, people learn better with something in front of them.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:44.050
People are different, so I won't deny that possibility.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:48.180
Basically, it doesn't matter what route you take.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:51.520
As long as you reach the same goal, it's okay.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:59.480
If you don't understand, that's fine.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:52.370
I believe it's a waste if you don't use all your tools.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.510
Yeah, you're right!

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:04.240
I finally found you after Kaho-chan came with me to look.

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:07.640
I even had Misa-san give you a chip.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.140
I can do it, too, right?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.150
Yeah.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:15.400
Okay.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.400
The cat-searching Code...

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.200
Cat-searching Code!

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.630
Morishita?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.090
Let me try one more time!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:56.400
Looks like I can't do it...

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.900
I see. So, you couldn't...

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.490
Yeah.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.060
I put a pretty strong Code in there, too.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.670
Well, it's to be expected...

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:26.360
I guess your summoning magic is really strong.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:40.300
I want to be like Misa-san and Yumiko-chan.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.110
You're completely mistaken

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:52.480
if you think just anyone can be good at magic simply by having tools.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:56.500
Sometimes, people learn better with something in front of them.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.680
Basically, it doesn't matter what route you take.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.510
As long as you reach the same goal, it's okay.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.520
I want to get better...

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:14.240
There!

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.520
One more time!

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.730
One more time!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.400
I'll try one more time.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.730
It's impossible.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.360
No matter what they do,

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.540
those who depend on tools won't get better.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.980
That might be true,

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:46.930
but this is the only thing I can do right now...

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:52.220
You were only able to use that staff after you'd put in the effort, right?

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:55.560
You learned to be good at magic, didn't you?

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:02.110
I want to be good, too, so I have to practice more.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:07.030
Why did you get into magic?

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.620
Why?

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:12.480
It's not really a reason...

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:13.840
Why?

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.560
Um, that's...

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.120
Um...

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:22.000
I never had any confidence in myself.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.630
No matter what I tried, I didn't keep going.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.000
Tennis...

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.410
Lacrosse...

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:33.030
The flute...

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:38.610
I got into high school and tried different things,

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.590
but I just caused people problems.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.890
So I ended up quitting each time.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.240
But...

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.610
"If you don't have confidence in yourself,

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.990
if you want to change yourself completely...

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.490
Anyone can do it..."

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:59.010
That was when I first came into contact with Modern-Day Magic.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:04.150
If it had to do with magic, I thought I might be able to get serious.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:09.050
I'm a klutz and slow, but I thought I'd try it.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:17.580
But it was a lie that anyone can do it.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.040
I have to work harder.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.740
Let's go.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:31.610
You won't find any cats if you stay here.

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:34.890
Right!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:43.070
The effective radius of the Code in your backpack is 500 meters.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:47.460
There's no point unless you execute it where the cats are.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.270
I see.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.200
Hello?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.690
Morishita, where are you?

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.860
Um... Ginza.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:02.130
I'm not sure what area.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.250
Kaho-chan, what are you doing?

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.930
I looked on the internet for the cat in the flyer.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:10.770
If they're willing to go as far as putting up a poster,

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:13.770
then they probably put one up on the net, too.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.190
There was some info.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:21.540
Thirty minutes ago, someone posted that they might have seen it at a Central Park bench.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:25.160
It shouldn't have gone far.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.010
I'll head there, too.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:29.930
Got it. Central Park, right?

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.520
Right.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:42.370
I wonder where it is...

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.780
Morishita, Ichinose.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.320
There was another post after that.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.600
Someone saw it around 3rd Street.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:53.630
That should be within 500 meters!

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Hurry and execute the cat-searching Code.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:56.660
Right!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.900
Morishita?

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:04.710
If you don't hurry up, the cat will go somewhere else!

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.210
I got it.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.030
But...

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:12.000
Koyomi, believe in yourself!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.050
You're a mage, right?

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.010
That's right...

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.980
You're right!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.880
I'm a mage!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:51.600
They're here.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.120
No way.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.220
He should be here.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.290
Yeah.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:05.790
There!

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.630
It's him!

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.670
Let's go home to your owner.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.650
What's up with all these cats?

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:14.880
Call the Department of Public Health!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.160
The Department of Public Health!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.860
Mom, I'm scared!

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:18.970
Are you okay?

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.640
There are a lot of them.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:22.940
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.200
The Code's out of control?

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:38.350
It's also the job of a mage to clean up the magic they use.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.140
B-But how?

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.920
Nullify the remaining Code.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.990
Just do what you always do.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:48.650
Yeah!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.790
Kaho-chan, hold him.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:55.650
Okay!

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.190
There!

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.830
Oh, it was just a street act.

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.460
You're good!

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.040
I did it!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:53.230
I thought I was a goner when the wash basin fell,

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:56.840
but all the cats started coming out!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:57.860
I see.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.090
Good for you.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:02.090
Yeah! Thanks!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:07.190
I'm going to try harder with Mr. Turtle!

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.620
You're still saying stuff like that.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.990
You're nuts.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:16.150
You're not in middle school anymore,

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.100
so enough with the silly delusions.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.330
They're not delusions! It's magic!

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.330
And that's what I mean by delusions.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.780
You guys want dinner?

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.900
Please!

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.530
I'll have some.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.560
Yeah.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.480
And the delusional middle schooler?

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:34.690
I'll have some.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.580
Wait, I'm not in middle school!

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:38.800
Then help me out.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.000
By the way,

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.390
about the Code Koyomi executed...

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:57.690
It should have only worked within a 500 meter radius,

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.400
so why did I detect it 2 kilometers away?

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:05.660
Who knows? I wonder why.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.480
I see.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.730
Anyway, what I have a problem with

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.290
is why that Code went out of control?

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:20.330
The Code in the chip is designed to detect and amplify Codes.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:28.570
Almost like you wanted to get Koyomi to use her summoning magic...

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.660
Really? I see.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:35.830
I told you, it's magic!

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.500
It's not fake!

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:45.530
I'm totally going to give it to Soshiro with my turtle!

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:54.040
M-My turtle...

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:07.010
You're so mean, Katamari!

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:11.030
My turtle!

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:48.730
Women are mysterious.

00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:52.680
That goes even more for beautiful Modern-Day mages.

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:56.170
Anehara Misa speculates on the Daemon-summoning incident,

00:23:56.170 --> 00:23:59.990
while dancing through the sky in a plane.

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:07.050
Spell = Code    #2

00:24:07.540 --> 00:24:10.060
Are you enjoying your summer vacation?

00:24:10.060 --> 00:24:12.100
Morishita Koyomi here.

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:15.340
Hi. By going out at night, you can avoid the heat.

00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:17.080
Anehara Misa here.

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:18.970
Continuing from last time,

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:21.980
we're going to be learning about Codes.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:25.750
Last time, we named spells "Codes."

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:28.370
This time, we're going to learn

00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:31.630
how to perform magic, using those Codes.

00:24:31.630 --> 00:24:35.510
Okay! Let's do it!

00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:37.480
First is Classical Magic.

00:24:37.480 --> 00:24:41.790
You construct Codes in the body and create magic that way.

00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:43.320
Inside your body?

00:24:43.320 --> 00:24:46.550
H-How do you do that?

00:24:46.550 --> 00:24:48.810
As we discussed last week,

00:24:48.810 --> 00:24:51.530
chanting a spell to heighten your consciousness,

00:24:51.530 --> 00:24:54.710
while running certain electrical signals through your body,

00:24:54.710 --> 00:24:59.020
forces a different world's laws to take precedence, basically effecting what you'd call magic.

00:24:59.020 --> 00:25:01.460
Essentially, that's a Classical Magic Code.

00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:03.660
I see.

00:25:03.660 --> 00:25:07.780
But you're using your own body to do it,

00:25:07.780 --> 00:25:10.210
so isn't that really difficult?

00:25:10.210 --> 00:25:11.650
You're right.

00:25:11.650 --> 00:25:14.460
The amount of stamina one has,

00:25:14.460 --> 00:25:19.820
the ability to focus, affinity for using Codes, and experience can all have a large effect.

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:20.810
For example,

00:25:20.810 --> 00:25:24.020
even with Yumiko, who's at the top of her class as a Classical Mage...

00:25:24.020 --> 00:25:28.290
If she uses magic when she's tired or weak,

00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:33.880
it's hard on her body, and she can even hurt herself with the magic.

00:25:35.880 --> 00:25:39.560
Classical Magic sounds really hard!

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:41.350
That's right.

00:25:41.350 --> 00:25:43.930
You're a pretty big klutz,

00:25:43.930 --> 00:25:47.150
so if you're going to learn Classical Magic, you should be careful.

00:25:47.150 --> 00:25:48.230
Okay!

00:25:48.230 --> 00:25:50.050
I'll be careful!

00:25:50.050 --> 00:25:51.600
One more thing.

00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:54.050
If you were to take Modern-Day Magic into consideration...

00:25:54.050 --> 00:25:57.440
Oh, it looks like we're out of time.

00:25:57.440 --> 00:25:58.670
Right!

00:25:58.670 --> 00:26:04.420
Okay, so next time, let's learn about Modern-Day Magic and Codes!

00:26:04.420 --> 00:26:05.450
Bye!

00:26:05.450 --> 00:26:07.740
Bye bye!
